@startuml user_flow_queue
!theme plain
title Experiment Queue – User Flow

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F5F8FA
  BorderColor #4A5568
}

[*] --> QueuePage

state QueuePage {
    state "Queue control bar" as Ctrl {
        Ctrl : Pause / Resume button
        Ctrl : Worker limit indicator
    }
    state "Active experiment panel" as Active {
        Active : Progress bar (run k/N, gen g/G)
        Active : Metric cards (best fitness, mean fitness, wall time)
        Active : Live stdout expander (tails _stdout.log)
        Active : Cancel button
    }
    state "All experiments table" as Table {
        Table : Status badge (queued / running / completed / failed / cancelled)
        Table : Algorithm + environment labels
        Table : Submission time
        Table : Delete button (terminal states only)
    }
    Ctrl --> Active : running experiment
    Ctrl --> Table
    Active --> Table
}

state "Experiment lifecycle" as Lifecycle {
    [*] --> Queued
    Queued --> Running : dispatcher dequeues
    Running --> Completed : runner exit 0
    Running --> Failed : runner exit ≠0
    Running --> Cancelled : user cancels (SIGTERM)
    Queued --> Cancelled : user cancels (skip)
}

note right of Active
  Polls every ~2s via st.rerun():
  • GET /queue -> paused/running/queued
  • GET /experiments/{id}/progress -> bar + metrics
  • GET /experiments/{id}/stdout -> log tail
  • GET /experiments -> table data
end note

note right of Lifecycle
  Queue-level pause:
  • Pause -> dispatcher stops dequeueing
  • Running experiment continues
  • Resume -> dispatcher resumes

  Cancel:
  • Queued -> status = cancelled (skip)
  • Running -> proc.terminate() (+ kill timeout)
  • Partial results preserved in experiment dir
end note

@enduml
